"""Roman Hinglish teaching notes for the user's eleven-slide presentation.

Examples labelled 'samjhane ke liye' are illustrations, not measured results.
"""
PAGES = []

def page(slide, title, *blocks, refs=()):
    PAGES.append(dict(slide=slide, title=title, blocks=list(blocks), refs=list(refs)))

page(1, 'SAFE-Pipe ka idea: pehle problem samjho',
('Ek familiar example', 'Socho ek company ke paas orders ki table hai. Usko city-wise total sales nikalni hain. Data ko read karna, group karna aur result banana ek processing job hai. Ab sawaal: is job ko kitne workers, kitne threads aur kitni memory dein? Kam resources dene se job slow ya fail ho sakti hai; zyada dene se configured resources ka kharcha badh sakta hai. Yeh example samjhane ke liye hai, hamara measured business dataset nahi.'),
('Hamne kya banaya?', 'SAFE-Pipe ek configuration advisor hai. Supported workload aur deadline do; yeh available settings ke runtime estimates banata hai, checks lagata hai, phir ek setting recommend karta hai. Suitable option nahi mila toh abstain karta hai: matlab recommendation dene se mana karta hai aur reason batata hai. Current advise command khud full Dask job launch nahi karta.'),
('Title ko chhote parts mein padho', '<b>Runtime optimization:</b> time ko decision mein lena. <b>Cost:</b> yahan configured thread/memory-time ka proxy, rupees ya AWS bill nahi. <b>SLA constraints:</b> declared time limit ke andar candidate hona. <b>Failure-aware:</b> unsuitable/unknown cases, pressure evidence aur failure handling ko ignore na karna. Iska matlab trained failure-probability model ready hona nahi hai.'),
('Slide ka research question', '"Can a short sample tell us how a full Dask job will behave?" baad ki research direction hai. Pehle runtime advisor bana; phir poocha ki chhota trial, ya probe, large job ki memory difficulty ko pehle expose kar sakta hai ya nahi. Current evidence ka answer conditional aur mostly negative hai: tested probes ne extra cost li, lekin stronger metadata se better choices demonstrate nahi ki.'),
('Viva mein aise bolo', '"Hum local Dask jobs ke liye resource settings suggest karte hain. Original advisor runtime predict karta hai. Later research mein humne test kiya ki small-sample execution se memory-related decisions improve hote hain ya nahi."'), refs=('M1','M4','R7'))

page(1, 'Task, job, worker, thread: sab alag hain',
('Job aur pipeline', '<b>Pipeline</b> steps ka sequence hai, jaise read -> clean -> join -> aggregate -> output. <b>Job</b> ek requested computation ka complete execution hai. Hamare benchmarks deliberately chhote operator-focused jobs hain; poora production ETL platform evaluate nahi hua.'),
('Task aur partition', '<b>Partition</b> data ka chunk hai. <b>Task</b> execution graph mein ek unit of work hai: ek chunk read karna, partial sum banana ya shuffle ka part karna. Ek job mein kai tasks ho sakte hain. 96 runs ka matlab 96 Dask tasks nahi; har run apna task graph execute karta hai.'),
('Scheduler aur worker', '<b>Scheduler</b> decide karta hai kaunsa ready task kis worker ko dena hai. <b>Worker</b> process task execute karta hai. <b>Thread</b> worker ke andar execution lane hai. Do workers aur har worker mein do threads ka matlab four configured lanes; actual CPU utilization exactly four cores jitna hona guaranteed nahi.'),
('Distributed naam, ek laptop ka experiment', 'Dask distributed execution support karta hai, lekin hamne LocalCluster se ek Windows PC par multiple processes chalaye. Isse scheduling, inter-process exchange aur worker limits test hue. Isko multi-machine cluster experiment kehna galat hoga. Actual host lagbhag 31.4 GiB RAM wala tha; worker caps jaan-boojhkar 1 GB/2 GB rakhe gaye.'),
('Ek chhota mental model', 'Restaurant analogy: poora order = job; chopping/boiling = tasks; ingredient trays = partitions; kitchen manager = scheduler; cooks = workers. Analogy mein threads ko work lanes samjho. Memory cap working space jaisa hai, lekin Dask cap hard reserved wall nahi hai. Aage memory page par iska exact matlab dekhenge.'), refs=('M1','M2'))

page(2, 'Timeline: hum kahaan se kahaan aaye?',
('1. Shuruaat: framework aur controlled data', 'Repository mein workload definitions, schemas, eight-setting grid, record store aur planner aaye. Windows par Dask setup verify hua, small pilots hue, phir four frozen synthetic datasets aur deadlines record kiye gaye. Frozen ka matlab is study ke liye identity/settings lock karna, taaki comparison mein inputs chupke na badlein.'),
('2. Midterm: original 96-run study', 'Four profiles ko eight configurations par three times chalaya: 4 x 8 x 3 = 96 physical runs. Sab successful hue aur engine deadlines ke andar the. Isi audited table ke grouped split se LightGBM runtime model, calibration margin aur baseline comparison bana. Prediction model poore data ki business rows nahi, run-summary rows par train hua.'),
('3. Advisor ko improve kiya', 'Balanced, fastest aur resource preference modes; exact-profile support; artifact identity checks; candidate-wise explanations; aur abstention implement hue. Existing model reuse hua. Policy selection ka formula badalne ka matlab har baar model retrain karna nahi hai.'),
('4. Research mein harder questions aaye', 'Bigger/uneven operator inputs par screen kiya; phir Stage A mein full-job pressure, Stage B mein matching small samples, phir worker-level telemetry aur one-probe economics inspect ki. Yeh original 96-row training table se separate studies hain.'),
('5. Ab ka checkpoint', 'Original-advisor completion branch par prospective validation ka software verified hai: 143 tests passed. Fresh 96 runs abhi start nahi hue. Research one-probe code ke 38 tests passed hain, lekin automatic probing disabled hai. Software readiness aur scientifically demonstrated performance do alag milestones hain.'), refs=('M1','M7','R1','R3','R4','R8'))

page(2, 'Git branches aur woh 6 GB wali baat',
('Branch ka simple meaning', 'Git repository project ki versioned history hai. Commit ek saved checkpoint hai. Branch development ki parallel line hai: team experimental changes ko stable work se alag rakh sakti hai. Branch banana data automatically duplicate karke benchmark chalana nahi hai; aur branch push karna main mein merge karna bhi nahi hai.'),
('Hamari teen relevant lines', '<b>main:</b> merged original advisor/study work. <b>codex/partition-probe-research:</b> separate probe experiments, memory exports, analyses aur guarded research prototype. <b>codex/main-advisor-completion:</b> original advisor ki fresh-validation infrastructure aur current report work. Research results report mein discuss karne se research code main advisor mein integrate nahi ho jata.'),
('6 GB database tha kya?', 'Earlier retained note mein lagbhag <b>6.78 GiB</b> prepared Parquet/sample storage across two screen directories tha. Yeh ek single training database, LightGBM model size, ya sirf 68 text log entries ka size nahi tha. Multiple full inputs aur sample variants disk par store hue the. Diagnostics aur logs bhi separate artifacts ho sakte hain; cited 6.78 GiB figure specifically prepared storage ka historical note hai, current disk inventory nahi.'),
('Disk, RAM aur model table ko mix mat karo', 'Disk par Parquet compressed files hain. RAM mein decoded tables, intermediate results aur buffers aa sakte hain. Curated runs.csv mein har run ka summary hai. LightGBM saved artifact learned trees rakhta hai. In chaar cheezon ka size ek doosre ke barabar nahi hota.'),
('Is guide ki evidence boundary', 'Original evidence caa8a8a aur research evidence edef1cd par pinned hai; current status 8179c07 ke baad local records se check hua. Later teammate changes is guide mein automatically reflect nahi honge. Source map mein exact files aur branch-specific Git links diye hain.'), refs=('M1','M10','R1'))

page(3, 'Architecture: offline learning aur online advice',
('Upar wali row: offline fit', '1. Fixed datasets banao aur identify karo. 2. Configurations par physical runs collect karo. 3. Runs ko audit karke train/calibration/test groups banao. 4. Model fit karo, upper multiplier calibrate karo. 5. Model, feature names aur support bindings save karo. Yeh expensive preparation phase hai; har recommendation par repeat nahi hota.'),
('Neeche wali row: per-request path', '1. User workload descriptors, SLA aur mode deta hai. 2. Advisor supported descriptor match check karta hai. 3. Same workload ke liye eight candidate settings ke feature rows banata hai. 4. Saved model se eight point estimates aur upper estimates nikalta hai. 5. Deadline/resource checks ke baad eligible choices score karta hai. 6. Winner ya abstention return hota hai.'),
('Bindings ka matlab', 'Model kisi specific feature/table/grid version ke saath fit hua tha. Bindings hashes aur identities se us relationship ko check karti hain. Agar config ID same ho lekin memory silently change ho jaye, old prediction ko trustworthy bolna theek nahi. Hash ek file fingerprint hai; experiment ka result correct hone ka mathematical proof nahi.'),
('Training aur inference mein farq', 'Training mein model known inputs aur measured runtimes se patterns seekhta hai. Inference mein saved model naye request-feature rows par predictions deta hai. Current request par model Dask execution dekhkar answer nahi banata. Actual runtime prediction ke baad full job chalne par hi pata lagega.'),
('Slide ki dono status strips', 'Fresh Windows validation protocol ready ka matlab collection/evaluation code available aur verified hai. Research automatic probing disabled ka matlab current default policy secretly sample job nahi chala rahi. Dono statements alag branches aur alag purposes ko refer karte hain.'), refs=('M3','M4','M7','R7'))

page(3, 'LightGBM ko exactly kya information milti hai?',
('Workload side ke six fields', '<b>family:</b> scan_filter/groupby/skewed_join/sort_merge. <b>input_bytes:</b> compressed input file bytes. <b>estimated_rows:</b> frozen row descriptor. <b>file_count:</b> declared files. <b>partition_count:</b> declared input partitions. <b>skew_score:</b> fixed family tag; current original model mein computed statistical skew measurement nahi.'),
('Configuration side ke six fields', '<b>config_id:</b> candidate ka naam. <b>n_workers:</b> worker processes. <b>threads_per_worker:</b> har worker ke threads. <b>memory_limit_gb:</b> frozen nominal memory encoding. <b>allocated_vcpus:</b> workers x threads, naam ke bawajood configured concurrency. <b>allocated_gb:</b> workers x nominal per-worker memory. Total twelve pre-run columns whitelist mein hain.'),
('Ek request ka example', 'sort_merge workload ki file size/rows/partition descriptors fixed rehte hain. Candidate A = w2_t2_1g, candidate B = w2_t2_2g. In dono feature rows mein configuration-related values change hote hain; workload fields same rehte hain. family aur config_id ko one-hot columns mein encode kiya jata hai: category ke liye 0/1 indicators.'),
('Kya model nahi dekhta?', 'Us target run ka actual engine_seconds, success/failure status, SLA miss aur peak memory prediction input nahi hain. Inhe pehle de dena future answer leak karna hoga. SLA aur preference mode advisor ki selection logic mein jaate hain; original twelve-feature runtime model ke input columns nahi hain.'),
('Ek important limitation', 'Current exact descriptor match four known profiles tak scope limit karta hai. Matching size/name alone actual file contents ya same hardware prove nahi karta. Original join ka row descriptor left side count hai; file_count right-side extra file omit karta hai. Frozen encoding ko bina versioning change nahi karte; guide mein is caveat ko slide 4 ke saath samjho.'), refs=('M2','M3','M4'))

page(3, 'Metadata profiling se execution profiling tak kyun?',
('Profiling = useful characteristics collect karna', 'Metadata profiling mein data ke baare mein information padho: size, rows, file/partition layout, schema. Sample execution profiling mein workload ka chhota version run karke time aur memory behavior observe karo. Dono profiling hain, lekin unki information aur cost alag hain.'),
('Original project ka profiler kya tha?', 'Original advisor ke descriptors kaafi had tak frozen manifests aur family tags se aate the. Isliye ise har arbitrary dataset ko deeply inspect karne wala universal profiler mat samjho. Example: skew_score original table mein family tag hai. Itna metadata supported fixed-profile runtime prediction ke liye use hua.'),
('Execution probe try karne ka reason', 'Same compressed bytes ka matlab same peak RAM nahi. Join, shuffle, key concentration aur uneven partitions different working sets bana sakte hain. Research question tha: agar chhota real run karein toh metadata se hidden memory difficulty ki extra information mil sakti hai? Yeh hypothesis tha, pehle se proven benefit nahi.'),
('Research ne kya sikhaya?', 'Small probes ka binary warning signal sab cases mein quiet tha. Later continuous peak/cap readings vary hui, lekin tested cases mein wahi split mila jo stronger metadata already identify kar raha tha. Isliye original metadata approach ko replace karne ka evidence nahi mila; probe-off decision reasonable raha.'),
('Apne words mein jawab', '"Hum metadata ko galat maan kar execution profiling par nahi gaye. Humne check kiya ki execution ki extra information uske extra time ke worth hai ya nahi. Current short workloads par benefit demonstrate nahi hua." Yeh honest explanation negative result ko bhi research ka useful output banati hai.'), refs=('M2','R4','R6','R7'))

page(4, 'Four workloads: actual code kya karta hai?',
('1. scan_filter', 'Files read hoti hain; value > 0.5 wali rows select hoti hain; selected value ka mean nikalta hai. Sochne ke liye: threshold se upar readings ka average. Repository mein generated flag column filter ke liye use nahi hota. Yahan read/filter/aggregate pattern measure hua.'),
('2. groupby', 'Rows ko key ke basis par groups mein baanto; har key ke value ka sum, phir sums ka mean. Example: city-wise sales totals. Same key ke records ko combine karne ki zaroorat different tasks/partitions ke data exchange ko relevant bana sakti hai.'),
('3. skewed_join', 'Left aur right table key par inner join hoti hain; joined payload ka sum calculate hota hai. Skew ka matlab kuch keys disproportionately frequent ho sakti hain. Example: kuch customer IDs par bahut saare orders. Original join aur later research join ki generation recipes alag hain; unke counts mix mat karo.'),
('4. sort_merge label', 'Is repository ka sort_merge workload set_index(key, shuffle="tasks") karta hai, phir har sorted partition se first payload value lekar scalar sum banata hai. Yeh shuffle force karta hai. Naam dekhkar isko second-table merge-sort algorithm ka benchmark mat batao: actual implementation key-based shuffle/index operation hai.'),
('Ek dataset ya multiple?', 'Original study mein <b>four separately generated frozen profiles/datasets</b> hain, har family ka ek. Same profile ko eight worker settings par rerun kiya. Dataset same rehne se configuration comparison cleaner hota hai. Later research mein additional generated instances aur samples aaye; project ke lifetime mein sirf ek dataset nahi raha.'), refs=('M2','M5'))

page(4, 'Data size, eight settings aur SLA',
('Slide ka table kaise padhein?', 'scan_filter: 23.32 million declared rows, 198.45 MB compressed input, 2.6 s SLA. groupby: 14.97 million, 198.49 MB, 7.9 s. skewed_join: 17.04 million left rows, 174.60 MB both-side bytes, 4.3 s. sort_merge: 12.77 million, 178.38 MB, 13.1 s. MB decimal hai; yeh disk bytes hain, RAM peak nahi.'),
('Join count ka hidden detail', 'Original join mein 17.04 million left rows ke alawa 852,000 right rows hain. 16 left files + 1 right file = 17 physical files. Slide ka declared rows label isi liye important hai: frozen features mein 16 files aur left-row count hai. Yeh caveat evidence explain karta hai; ab old fitted inputs silently repair nahi kiye jaate.'),
('Eight configurations kaise banti hain?', 'Workers {1,2} x threads per worker {1,2} x memory per worker {1 GB,2 GB} = 8. IDs: w1_t1_1g, w1_t1_2g, w1_t2_1g, w1_t2_2g, w2_t1_1g, w2_t1_2g, w2_t2_1g, w2_t2_2g. w2_t2_1g = two worker processes, each two threads, each 1 GB cap: four threads aur 2 GB total configured cap.'),
('SLA kahaan se aaya?', 'Original separate pilots mein w1_t1_2g ke three engine timings ka median liya, 1.5 se multiply kiya, phir next 0.1 second tak round up karke deadlines freeze ki. Yeh company ke real customer contract se li hui deadlines nahi; study ke predeclared engine deadlines hain.'),
('Memory cap ka precise wording', '2 GB total cap ko "system ne exactly 2 GB RAM reserve kar li" mat bolo. Yeh configured worker limits ka sum hai. Actual memory use lower ya transiently higher ho sakta hai; scheduler/client/other process memory bhi hoti hai. Slide 2 ki reserves-more-RAM wording ko explain karte waqt configured allowance bolo.'), refs=('M2','M5','M4'))

page(4, '96 runs ka denominator aur timing boundary',
('Group aur run ka farq', 'Ek family/config pair ko original model split mein group ya cell kehte hain. Four families x eight configs = 32 groups. Har group ke three repeats = 96 executions. Kuch planner files repeat ko include karke 96 planned cells bolti hain. Presentation mein "96 runs across 32 profile/config groups" sabse clear hai.'),
('Three repeats kyun?', 'Background processes, cache, startup aur normal execution variability time ko affect kar sakte hain. Repeats se ek observed range aur median milta hai. Lekin same dataset ko three times chalane se three independent new workloads nahi bante. Independent scope evidence ke liye different untouched instances chahiye.'),
('Engine time versus total waiting time', 'Original engine_seconds cluster/client creation ke baad graph construction se scalar completion tak measure hota hai. Dataset generation, cluster startup/teardown aur profiling is timer mein nahi hain. Isliye 2.6-second engine SLA ka matlab user click se complete response 2.6 seconds mein aana nahi.'),
('96/96 ka valid meaning', 'Original scored executions sab success the aur apni engine deadlines meet ki. Is table mein failure variation nahi tha, aur original peak_memory_bytes missing the. Isliye na failure classifier train hua, na original table se measured peak-memory prediction accuracy claim kar sakte hain.'),
('Slide explain karte waqt', '"Humne settings ka controlled grid run kiya. All 96 jobs succeeded, lekin yeh four fixed profiles aur one Windows host ka result hai. Yeh arbitrary input ke liye universal safety proof nahi hai." Data dictionary kholkar status, sla_miss aur missing peak-memory columns ka meaning check kar sakte ho.'), refs=('M2','M6'))
page(5, 'LightGBM: model seekhta kya hai?',
('Decision trees ka simple idea', 'Ek decision tree input fields par chhote questions poochkar prediction banata hai: family kya hai, workers kitne hain, memory setting kya hai? Boosting mein multiple trees milkar previous prediction ki error reduce karne ki koshish karte hain. LightGBM gradient-boosted trees ki implementation hai. Hamne regression use ki: output continuous runtime hai, yes/no class nahi.'),
('Training data ka ek row', 'Ek benchmark run summary mein profile descriptors, configuration aur measured engine_seconds hota hai. Features model ko diye gaye; engine_seconds learning target tha. Millions of Parquet records directly model ke millions of training examples nahi bane. Original model fit mein sirf 36 run-summary rows the.'),
('Log-runtime kyun?', 'Code log(engine_seconds) ko predict karta hai, phir exp() se seconds mein wapas aata hai. Log scale relative differences ko represent karne mein useful ho sakti hai aur exponentiation positive output deta hai. Is engineering choice ko hamari table se universally best transformation prove nahi kiya gaya. Output point estimate hai, guaranteed actual time nahi.'),
('Actual fixed settings', '120 trees; maximum seven leaves per tree; learning rate 0.05; minimum child samples three; L2 regularization one; random seed 2026; one training thread. Learning rate har boosting update ka step size hai; leaves/tree complexity control karte hain; regularization fitting ko restrain karti hai. Yeh settings code mein fixed hain, archived hyperparameter search ka winning result nahi.'),
('Isko kyun choose kiya?', 'Structured tabular features ke liye boosted trees ek practical engineering option the. Recorded comparison simple family-median baseline ke against hai. XGBoost, neural network ya har possible model ko beat karne ka evidence nahi hai. Research probe branch mein yeh model dobara train nahi hua.'), refs=('M3','M8','E2'))

page(5, 'Train, calibration aur test: teen alag roles',
('Training: prediction seekhna', '12 family/config groups x three repeats = 36 rows model fitting ke liye. Model in features aur known runtime ke relationships learn karta hai. Same family ki other configuration groups calibration/test mein ho sakti hain.'),
('Calibration: margin set karna', 'Alag 12 groups / 36 rows use hue. Fitted model ki log-prediction errors se upper estimate ka multiplier choose hua. Har group ka maximum residual liya; negative residuals pehle se discard karne ka rule nahi tha. Calibration model ke trees ko train nahi karti; prediction par margin calculate karti hai.'),
('Test: saved choices ke baad check', 'Bache eight groups / 24 rows par final error aur upper coverage report hue. Is test ko prediction fitting ya margin setting ke liye use nahi karna chahiye. Counts 36 + 36 + 24 = 96; yeh usual 80/20 split nahi hai.'),
('Repeats ko saath kyun rakha?', 'Maan lo groupby + w2_t1_1g ko three times run kiya. Agar repeat 1 train aur repeat 2 test mein aa gaya, almost same situation dono sides par hogi. Grouped split us exact family/config pair ke saare repeats ek side rakhta hai. Isse repeat leakage avoid hoti hai.'),
('Phir bhi kya limit hai?', 'Train/calibration/test sab mein same four frozen workload profiles ka scope hai. Test new dataset size, new workload family ya new computer ka test nahi hai. Grouping useful hai, lekin statistical exchangeability automatically prove nahi karti. Exchangeability ko simple words mein future examples aur calibration examples ka comparable distribution samjho; assumption fail ho toh coverage interpretation weak hoti hai.'), refs=('M3','M8','M9'))

page(5, '13.84% MdAPE ko example se samjho',
('Pehle ek prediction ka error', 'Absolute percentage error = abs(predicted - actual) / actual x 100. Samjhane ke liye: actual 10 s aur prediction 12 s ho toh error 20%. Prediction 8 s ho toh bhi absolute error 20%; absolute sign direction hata deta hai. Yeh example measured project row nahi hai.'),
('Median ka matlab', 'Har test row ka percentage error nikalo, values sort karo aur middle value lo. Even count mein middle two ka average hota hai. Samjhane ke liye errors 5%, 10%, 20%, 30%, 100% ka median 20% hai. Median extreme errors se mean ke comparison mein kam move hota hai, lekin worst-case error chhupa bhi sakta hai.'),
('Hamare actual result', '24 held-out rows par LightGBM MdAPE 13.842297%, slide par 13.84%. Same training split ka family-median baseline 23.013084%, slide par 23.01%. Difference about 9.17 percentage points hai. Yeh all-time/all-dataset guarantee nahi, saved test set ka result hai.'),
('Baseline kaise predict karta hai?', 'Har family ke training runtimes ka median lo. Us family ki test row ko wahi fixed number do, configuration ka detailed effect model na karo. LightGBM candidate fields use kar sakta hai; is comparison mein uska typical absolute relative error lower nikla. Yeh baseline ko fair same-training-data reference banata hai.'),
('Graph kaise padho?', 'Left bar chart mein shorter error bar better. Right scatter mein x actual seconds aur y predicted seconds hai. Dashed y=x line par exact prediction hoti. Above line = overprediction; below line = underprediction. Nearby repeated points independent new workloads nahi hain. "86.16% accurate" mat bolo: 100 minus MdAPE classification accuracy nahi banata.'), refs=('M3','M9'))

page(5, '1.688 x t: upper estimate kaise bana?',
('Point estimate aur upper estimate', 'Point t model ka central runtime estimate hai. Upper U = t x exp(q), jahan q calibration residual offset hai. Saved q about 0.523642, isliye multiplier about 1.688. Samjhane ke liye t=2 s ho toh U about 3.376 s. Isko observed-data-based margin samjho, promise nahi.'),
('Calibration steps', 'Har calibration row ke liye log(actual runtime) minus log prediction nikalo. Har family/config group ke three repeats mein largest residual lo: 36 rows se 12 group scores. Nominal alpha=0.1 par rank ceil((12+1) x 0.9)=12 aata hai, toh largest of those 12 scores choose hua. Isse multiplier nikla.'),
('24/24 covered ka meaning', 'Held-out 24 rows mein har measured runtime us row ke upper estimate ke andar tha; group level par 8/8 covered. Yeh upper estimate ka coverage check hai, model ki exact prediction accuracy nahi. U broad ho toh coverage achhi ho sakti hai par usable deadline eligibility tight ho sakti hai.'),
('Isse 100% guarantee kyun nahi?', 'Sirf eight test groups, same four profiles aur one host hain. Future hardware, input layout, software ya workload change ho sakta hai. Grouping repetitions alone comparable future distribution establish nahi karti. Selected winning configuration ke liye universal 90% completion guarantee bhi is result se nahi milti.'),
('Advisor mein U ka use', 'Deadline D ho toh upper estimate deadline ke andar honi chahiye. Point estimate score/ranking mein use hota hai. Same 1.688 multiplier sab candidates par hai; yeh separately different failure probabilities estimate nahi karta. "Margin ke saath eligible" kehna "job guaranteed safe" se more accurate hai.'), refs=('M3','M4','M8','M9'))

page(6, 'Balanced objective: formula ko words mein padho',
('Pehle eligible, phir cheapest score', 'Advisor pehle support, deadline aur budgets check karta hai. Ineligible candidate score achha hone par bhi choose nahi hota. Bache candidates ka J compare hota hai. Objective ka matlab declared preference: time aur configured resources ko kis balance mein value dena hai.'),
('Symbols ka matlab', '<b>t:</b> predicted engine seconds. <b>D:</b> requested engine deadline. <b>P:</b> workers x threads per worker. <b>M:</b> total configured worker cap. <b>lambda:</b> resource component mein thread share. <b>beta:</b> overall score mein latency share. Defaults lambda=0.5 aur balanced beta=0.5; yeh trained parameters nahi, preferences hain.'),
('Q: resource size ko normalize karo', 'Q = lambda x P/4 + (1-lambda) x M/4 GB. Grid ka maximum four configured threads aur four decimal GB hai. Divide karne se thread aur memory terms comparable dimensionless quantities bante hain. Reference values fixed hain; rejected options remove karne se baaki candidate ka score rescale nahi hota.'),
('R aur J', 'R = (t/D) x Q: time ke saath configured resource burden combine hota hai. J = beta x (t/D) + (1-beta) x R. Balanced mode dono parts ko weight deta hai. Fastest beta=1 se t/D minimize karta hai. Resource beta=0 se R minimize karta hai; sirf smallest RAM setting choose karna resource mode ki complete definition nahi.'),
('Score ko kya mat samjho', 'J rupees, electricity, actual CPU usage ya measured peak RAM nahi. 50/50 weights best possible scientifically optimized choice prove nahi hue. Formula transparent hai aur user preference represent karta hai; uski independent outcome benefit ko fresh study assess karegi.'), refs=('M4',))

page(6, 'Worked example: 2 GB total kyun select hua?',
('Candidate A: balanced winner', 'w2_t2_1g: workers=2, threads each=2, cap each=1 GB. Isliye P=4, M=2 GB. Saved point prediction about 2.29 s. D=13.1 s. Rounded numbers se Q=0.5 x 1 + 0.5 x 0.5 = 0.75. t/D about 0.1748; R about 0.1311; J about 0.1530.'),
('Candidate B: fastest winner', 'w2_t2_2g: same four threads, M=4 GB. Point about 2.15 s. Q=1; t/D about 0.1641; R about 0.1641; J about 0.1641. B time mein thoda faster hai, lekin configured memory double hai. Balanced score A ka lower hai, isliye A wins. Calculations rounded slide values se illustrative recomputation hain.'),
('Trade-off ka simple meaning', 'Prediction mein around 0.14 second difference hai. Declared balanced preference 2 GB extra configured cap ke badle itni small speed gain ko choose nahi karti. Isse actual 0.14 s saving measure nahi hui; yeh model predictions compare ho rahi hain. Fastest mode mein preference badalti hai, toh B win karta hai.'),
('Resource mode aur total/per-worker units', 'Saved resource-mode example w1_t2_1g choose karta hai: one worker, two threads, 1 GB total. Slide title ka 2 GB versus 4 GB <b>total</b> cap hai. Stage A ka 1 GB versus 2 GB <b>per worker</b> hai. Dono slides ke memory numbers same unit scope mein nahi hain.'),
('Viva answer', '"Sabse fast option aur balanced option alag ho sakte hain. Hum eligible settings ke point runtime aur configured resource-time trade-off ko declared weights se compare karte hain. Is sort example mein smaller total cap ka balanced score lower tha."'), refs=('M4','M11'))

page(6, 'Chart, eligibility aur abstention',
('Horizontal plot ko kaise read karein?', 'Har line ek candidate hai. Dot point prediction t; end tick upper estimate U; orange vertical line deadline 13.1 s. Dot-to-tick line error-bar confidence interval ki generic drawing nahi, yahan point-to-upper segment hai. Highlighted candidate balanced winner hai.'),
('Is example mein red rejection kyun nahi?', 'All eight candidates ke upper estimates 13.1-second deadline ke andar hain aur resource checks pass hue. Isliye yahan selection eligibility ke baad score se decide hoti hai. "Red candidates reject hue" is particular example ka explanation nahi hona chahiye.'),
('Hard checks', 'Exact supported workload descriptors aur artifact bindings match karein; U deadline ke andar ho; optional total-thread/total-memory budget pass ho; coarse input-bytes guard pass ho. Optional deadline reserve extra headroom maang sakta hai. Compressed size ka guard actual per-worker RAM safety proof nahi hai.'),
('0.01-second SLA par kya hota hai?', 'Itni tight deadline mein koi upper estimate pass nahi hoti; advisor abstain karta hai. Matlab "is scope/grid mein suitable suggestion nahi". Yeh crash nahi, deliberate outcome hai. Unknown profile par abstain hona bhi valid hai; unsupported data ko forcibly closest category banana evidence ko overstate karega.'),
('Prediction aur execution ko alag rakho', 'Saved advisor JSON recommendation aur comparison dikhata hai. It does not prove selected configuration abhi full data par run hui. Isi gap ko fresh prospective validation aur later exact-input execution binding address karenge. Evidence viewer ko complete product UI mat bolo.'), refs=('M4','M11'))

page(7, 'Research screen: chaar methods, teen actual probes',
('Probe ki definition', 'Full job start karne se pehle input ke smaller sample par same type ka processing run karna execution probe hai. Usse time/memory behavior ka cheap signal lene ki koshish hoti hai. Cheap relative term hai: agar full job bhi few seconds ka ho, probe ka setup usse mehenga pad sakta hai.'),
('Method 1: full', 'Complete input declared target memory cap par run hota hai. Yeh reference hai jiske against sample result compare karte hain. Isko small probe mat gino. Initial table mein four methods likhe hain, lekin scientifically one full reference + three sample-based methods hain.'),
('Method 2: uniform', 'Fact rows ka exact random quarter, same target worker cap. Samjhane ke liye 100 fact rows mein se 25 randomly select. Fayda simple representative sampling attempt; problem smaller input ke paas per-row zyada memory headroom ho sakta hai, toh full pressure disappear ho sakta hai.'),
('Method 3: uniform_memory', 'Wahi uniform sample files, lekin worker cap bhi fixed floor plus fraction scaling se reduce hota hai. Is comparison mein sample data same hai, memory allowance change hai. Intention: smaller input ko unrealistically easy memory environment na dena. Yeh mathematical equivalence ya guaranteed pressure preservation nahi.'),
('Method 4: partition_tail', 'Same total fact-row budget, lekin larger input partitions se preferential sampling. Worker cap mapping uniform_memory jaisi. Idea uneven input chunks ko better represent karna. Larger input file hot key ya expensive post-shuffle partition ke barabar nahi. Join ka dimension full retain hua, isliye matched fact rows ka matlab matched total bytes nahi.'), refs=('R1',))

page(7, 'Screen ka design aur usse kya mila?',
('768 attempts kaise bane?', 'Two families x three sizes x two patterns = 12 instances. Har instance par eight configurations, two repeats aur four methods: 12 x 8 x 2 x 4 = 768. Ismein 192 full references aur 576 sample-probe executions hain. Yeh original 96-run study se separate development screen hai.'),
('Recorded outcomes', '759 successes, one timeout, eight execution/worker errors. Timeout ko successful runtime nahi bana sakte. Failures ko drop karke best results present karna galat hota. Different attempts ki condition/evidence records preserve kiye gaye; unattended clean completion ko assume nahi kiya gaya.'),
('Ranking ka research question', 'Full data par candidate A fastest hai, kya small sample par bhi A fastest dikhta hai? Agar order flip ho gaya toh sample se selected configuration poor ho sakti hai. Ranking fidelity means ordering kitni preserve hui. Regret = sample-selected config ka full runtime best full runtime se kitna worse tha, relative percentage mein.'),
('Actual descriptive ranking results', 'Ten complete instances par median engine regret uniform 3.87%, uniform_memory 0.11%, partition_tail 8.17% tha. Yeh memory-scaled method ki universal victory nahi: other instances incomplete/failed the, means/maxima alag the, aur selected full historical failures bhi preserve hue. Tail heuristic ne automatically better representation prove nahi ki.'),
('Kyun Stage A par gaye?', 'Initial uneven patterns mein key skew aur file imbalance combined ho sakte the. Screen ne suggest kiya ki mechanism aur cost ko separate study chahiye. Har configuration par many probes run karke selection karna lifecycle/preparation mein costly tha. Sirf low engine regret dekhkar online savings declare nahi kar sakte.'), refs=('R1','R2'))

page(7, 'Stage A: key skew aur partition imbalance',
('Two independent knobs', '<b>Key skew:</b> some keys bahut frequent. Example 100 orders mein 60 ek customer ke. <b>Partition imbalance:</b> input chunks unequal. Example four files mein 10, 10, 10, 70 rows. Keys balanced ho sakti hain phir bhi file uneven; files equal ho sakti hain phir bhi ek key frequent. Yeh examples illustrations hain.'),
('Four patterns', 'Balanced: dono knobs off. Key-skew-only: frequent-key knob on. Partition-imbalance-only: uneven-file knob on. Both: dono on. Actual recipe seed 911, 2 million fact rows, eight fact files, sixteen payload columns; skew knob hot_fraction=0.25 aur imbalance parameter=0.60. Parameter ko direct measured file-share percentage mat samjho; generator layout matter karta hai.'),
('48 full runs', 'Two families groupby/join x four patterns = eight instances. Two configs w2_t1_1g/w2_t1_2g x three repeats = 48. Concurrency fixed: two workers, one thread each. Sirf per-worker cap compare hui: 1 GB versus 2 GB. Same dataset per instance reuse hua.'),
('Heatmap padho', 'Har cell ka 3/3 = three successful repeats, 0/3 = none successful. 1 GB par groupby partition-imbalance-only 0/3; join partition-imbalance-only 2/3; join both 0/3. Baaki low-cap patterns 3/3. 2 GB column sab 3/3. Total 1 GB 17/24, 2 GB 24/24, combined 41/48.'),
('Surprise ko hide mat karo', 'Groupby both 3/3 success tha, jabki partition-imbalance-only 0/3. Both case mein pressure/spill tha, so success aur quiet same nahi. Isse simple "more skew always worse" explanation reject hoti hai. One seed aur three repeats se exact causal mechanism establish nahi hota; observed outcomes clearly report karte hain.'), refs=('R3',))

page(7, '1 GB limit ke bawajood spill ya termination kaise?',
('RAM aur disk ka relation', 'Spill ka matlab worker data ka kuch hissa RAM se disk par temporarily rakhna. File disk par pehle se thi phir bhi intermediate results RAM use kar sakte hain. Cap Dask ka management target hai, hard operating-system reservation nahi. Data decode, join/shuffle buffers aur running tasks transient memory increase kar sakte hain.'),
('Default thresholds ka short map', 'Dask docs ke defaults: managed memory around 60% par spill target; process RSS around 70% par aggressive spill; 80% par new tasks pause; 95% par nanny worker terminate/restart kar sakti hai. Running work turant vanish nahi hota. Thresholds configurable hain; hamare termination analysis mein retained 0.95 threshold use hua. [E1]'),
('Nanny kya hai?', 'Dask nanny worker process ko supervise karti hai. Excess memory observe hone par worker stop/restart ho sakta hai; job kuch tasks recompute karke still finish kar sakti hai. Nanny termination ko automatically operating-system OOM kill mat bolo. Seven Stage A errors ke saath nanny memory-termination evidence tha.'),
('Disk size se peak RAM kyun nahi pata?', 'Compressed Parquet size, decoded in-memory arrays, temporary copies, shuffle buffers aur working set different cheezein hain. Particular operation aur partition layout matter karte hain. "200 MB file hai, 1 GB cap hai, toh always safe" valid rule nahi. More total RAM bhi ek single worker ke local peak ko eliminate nahi karti.'),
('Slide ke claim ka scope', '"All seven full-job errors occurred at 1 GB per worker" Stage A ke 48 attempts ka statement hai. Earlier 768-screen ke eight errors alag count hain. Higher cap tested cases mein worked, lekin har future input ke liye 2 GB enough ka result nahi hai.'), refs=('R3','R6','E1'))
page(8, 'Stage B: full jobs ke matching samples',
('Stage A aur B ka relationship', 'Stage A ne eight instances ke full outcomes diye. Stage B ne unhi parent inputs ke smaller samples check kiye. Ab question fastest ranking se narrow ho gaya: kya cheap sample warning full-input pressure ko reveal karti hai? Stage B mein initial screen ke saare methods dobara compare nahi hue.'),
('Only uniform_memory, two fractions', 'Stage B methods uniform_memory_f0125 aur uniform_memory_f0250 hain: fact rows ka 1/8 = 12.5% aur 1/4 = 25%. Eight instances x two target caps x two fractions x three repeats = 96 probes. Per instance/fraction ek deterministic sample bana; same sample caps aur repeats ke across reuse hua. Dono fractions nested hone ki guarantee nahi.'),
('Effective cap ka calculation', 'Formula: floor + fraction x (target cap - floor), rounded bytes. Floor = 512 MiB = 536,870,912 bytes. 1 GB target, quarter fraction: 536,870,912 + 0.25 x (1,000,000,000 - 536,870,912) = 652,653,184 bytes. Eighth fraction cap 594,762,048 bytes. Probe denominator actual effective cap hai, full target 1 GB nahi.'),
('Floor kyun rakha?', 'Intention fixed process overhead ko entirely fraction se shrink na karna tha. Lekin 512 MiB measured clean interpreter overhead nahi; fixed heuristic parameter hai. Fact rows, join dimension aur temporary memory linear ratio mein scale hona proven nahi. Right join dimension full retain hui, so quarter fact sample quarter total working set nahi.'),
('Quiet ka exact meaning', 'Success + complete clean diagnostics + declared spill/pause/restart/termination warning signals zero. Missing data ko quiet ya zero treat nahi karte. All 96 probes is declared rule se quiet the. Yeh observation ki quality definition hai, full job safety certificate nahi.'), refs=('R4','R5'))

page(8, '8/32 mismatch: iska actual meaning',
('32 groups ka denominator', 'Eight instances x two target caps x two fractions = 32 comparison groups. Har group mein three probe repeats hain. Separate sessions ke full repeat 1 aur sample repeat 1 ko exact synchronized pair nahi samjha. Comparison group level par full-reference pressure evidence ke saath hua.'),
('Cross marks wale eight cells', 'Low 1 GB cap par four cases: groupby partition-imbalance-only; groupby both; join partition-imbalance-only; join both. In four cases ko two sample fractions par compare kiya: 4 x 2 = 8. Full input mein warning/pressure thi, sample quiet raha. Yeh eight independent workload discoveries nahi hain.'),
('Pressure aur failure ka farq', 'Groupby both full 3/3 successful tha, lekin pressure/spill tha. Join partition-only full 2/3 successful tha, phir bhi pressure evidence tha. Isliye slide "missed pressure" kehti hai, "eight failed full jobs" nahi. 8/32 ko 25% future failure probability kehna bhi galat hai.'),
('Binary signal mein problem', 'Agar har probe ka answer quiet hai, toh us yes/no signal se difficult aur easy cases distinguish nahi hote. Stage B ke frozen time/resource rule ne har case mein 1 GB target select kiya. Historical selected full successes 17/24 rahe, jabki fixed 2 GB aur metadata reference 24/24 the. Yeh reused Stage A outcomes ka descriptive replay hai.'),
('Kya samples always useless hain?', 'Nahi. Result tested fraction, cap mapping, operator recipes aur one-seed cases ka hai. Continuous memory reading useful pattern dikha sakti thi, jo next review mein check hua. Lekin binary success ya no-warning alone ko full safety ka substitute banana is table mein supported nahi.'), refs=('R4','R5','R6'))

page(8, '37 worker lifetimes: graph ka confusion door karo',
('Run aur lifetime alag units', 'Stage A 48 + Stage B 96 = 144 jobs. Initially two workers each ka expectation 288 lifetimes hai. Export mein 321 distinct lifetimes retained: Stage A 129 (96 initial + 33 added), Stage B 192 initial. Added lifetime ko silently old worker peak mein merge nahi kiya; exact replacement pairing infer nahi ki.'),
('37 ka matlab', '37 distinct Stage A lifetimes ke saath nanny memory-termination events attributed hue. Yeh 37 failed jobs nahi: Stage A failed jobs only seven the. Ek job mein multiple workers terminate ho sakte hain; successful job recovery ke baad complete ho sakti hai. Added-lifetime count aur event count same quantity nahi hain.'),
('Graph ki axes aur marks', 'X-axis terminated lifetimes ko sampled peak ratio ke order mein dikhati hai; time axis nahi. Y-axis RSS / effective worker cap hai. Blue sampled peak saved periodic readings ka maximum; green nanny-event mark termination ke waqt logged reading; dashed line 0.95 threshold. Vertical separation shows retained sample peak aur event reading ka difference.'),
('Actual findings', '33/37 lifetimes mein saved peak 0.95 cap se below tha. Event RSS 36/37 mein saved peak se higher tha. All 37 attributed event readings threshold se above the. Event last retained sample ke 0.016-0.419 s baad tha; median gap 0.165 s. Brief spike ya last sample persist na hona consistent explanations hain, exact mechanism isolated nahi.'),
('Simple analogy', 'Har few moments mein speedometer photo lo. Photos mein max 80 ho, lekin beech mein meter 100 gaya ho sakta hai. Photo maximum continuous true maximum nahi. Isi tarah saved peak ko exact full-memory requirement training label nahi bana sakte. Event reading bhi ek observation hai, perfect continuous maximum nahi.'), refs=('R6',))

page(8, 'Memory fields aur continuous signal',
('Measurements ko alag pehchano', '<b>RSS:</b> process ki resident memory observation. <b>Managed memory:</b> Dask-tracked in-memory data estimate. <b>Spill:</b> disk par offloaded data evidence. <b>Baseline RSS:</b> first retained sample, guaranteed clean idle measurement nahi. <b>Peak RSS:</b> measurement window ke retained samples ka max. <b>Cap:</b> configured limit, measured consumption nahi.'),
('Export mein kya preserve kiya?', 'Run/cell identity, workload/config/fraction/repeat, effective cap, baseline/peak RSS, managed/spill peaks, sample count/errors/window, thresholds, status aur restart/termination evidence. Missing values missing hi rakhe. Restarted workers separate lifetimes rahe. Source plan/raw-record hashes checked hue; export banana benchmark rerun nahi tha.'),
('Binary quiet ke beyond q ratio', 'Per run q = largest individual worker sampled_peak_RSS / that worker effective cap. Individual quarter-size low-target probes mein historical quiet-full cases ratios 41.1-48.1%; pressure-full cases 59.1-67.6%. Yeh development table mein separation hai, future classifier accuracy nahi. Repeats across same sample independent workloads nahi.'),
('Phir probe use kyun nahi kiya?', 'Signal same four imbalanced-file instances separate kar raha tha jo metadata baseline already identify kar sakti thi. Extra measurement ne additional choice benefit show nahi kiya. Information present hona aur decision improve hona alag hai. Cost pay karke same answer milna short jobs ke liye weak proposition tha.'),
('Do common traps', 'Different workers ke lifetime peaks add karke concurrent cluster peak mat bolo: peaks same instant par nahi hue. Zero sampling errors ka matlab no missed spikes nahi. First RSS ko fixed overhead samajhkar old 512 MiB floor replace karna bhi validated method nahi. These details prevent neat-but-wrong memory claims.'), refs=('R6','R7'))

page(9, 'Cost gate: probe ka kharcha recover hua?',
('Gate ka seedha meaning', 'Gate = aage badhne ki condition. Yahan do sawaal the: probe metadata se extra useful decision information dega? Aur us information se milne wala possible benefit probe ki full cost se bada hoga? Current eight short-job instances mein dono milkar convincing benefit show nahi hua.'),
('Bars ka meaning', 'Size-aware metadata aur guarded default: 4.79 s median reconstructed request time. Fixed 2 GB: 4.96 s. Ambiguous-only one probe: 7.38 s. Always one probe: 10.37 s. Yeh actual online controller ke freshly measured end-to-end requests nahi; existing full/probe records ko accounting rules se combine karke replay numbers hain.'),
('Choices kya change hui?', 'Stronger metadata aur probe rules ne same eight instances ke liye same configs choose kiye: four ko 1 GB, four ko 2 GB. Selected historical full outcomes 24 unique references (eight x three) sab successful the. Repeated counterfactual exposure ko 72 independent full runs nahi gina.'),
('Simple calculation', '10.37 minus 4.79 = 5.58 s difference between reported medians. Separately per-instance single-probe preparation plus lifecycle/preflight ka median 5.47 s tha. Yeh numbers exactly equal hona required nahi: median(A+B) generally median(A)+median(B) nahi hota. 4.79 s metadata file read time bhi nahi; selected full job included hai.'),
('Decision kyun off raha?', 'Same choice, additional paid time, no demonstrated incremental benefit. Gate closed rakhna project failure hide karna nahi, evidence-following result hai. Longer jobs ya repeated-job reuse different use cases ho sakte hain, but unke fair baselines aur fresh measurements chahiye; yeh slide unhe prove nahi karti.'), refs=('R7',))

page(9, 'One-probe prototype exactly kaise sochta hai?',
('Stronger metadata estimate', 'Prototype fact/dimension rows, numeric payload count aur largest fact-file rows use karta hai. Approx dense bytes D = 8 x (payload columns+1) x fact rows + 16 x dimension rows. Largest fact partition L = 8 x (payload columns+1) x largest-file rows. Yeh input-layout arithmetic hai, actual measured RSS prediction model nahi.'),
('Lower/upper scenarios', 'Two workers ke liye Mlo = 128 MiB + D/2 + L; Mhi = 128 MiB + D/2 + 3L. Mhi <= 0.7 x 1 GB toh 1 GB; warna <= 0.7 x 2 GB toh 2 GB; otherwise abstain. Copy factors, reserve aur 0.7 threshold hand-set development heuristics hain, statistical confidence bounds nahi.'),
('Probe hota toh kya observe karta?', 'Diagnostic path one quarter-size uniform sample, two single-thread workers, low-target effective cap 652,653,184 bytes leta hai. Exactly one valid observation ki quality/identity check hoti hai. Clean observation ka q < 0.55 toh lower cap; otherwise higher cap. Cutoff 0.55 development separation dekhkar choose hua, independent calibrated threshold nahi.'),
('Current actual behavior', 'admission_enabled=false hai. Default metadata choose karta hai ya abstain; physical probe launch nahi hota. Existing-record counterfactual helper "agar yeh one observation aati toh?" check karta hai. It cannot secretly generate datasets, start Dask, train LightGBM ya execute proposed pilot.'),
('Unknown data par kya?', 'Missing sample fields, wrong dataset identity, warning/restart evidence ya unsuitable cost case lower-cap override justify nahi karte. Counterfactual diagnostic choice aur admission permission separate concepts hain. The proposed 48-attempt pilot disabled draft hai; ise completed Stage A 48 runs se mix mat karo.'), refs=('R7','R8','R9'))

page(9, 'Profiling mein extra time kahaan lagta hai?',
('Timer ko pieces mein tod do', 'Sample prepare/read/write karna; parent/sample identity preflight; fresh cluster aur Python workers start; libraries initialize; task graph build/schedule; sample operation execute; telemetry collect/persist; workers/cluster clean up. In sab ka total tiny engine computation se bada ho sakta hai. Full-input generation aur research-wide integrity audits experiment setup hain, har online request ki profiling cost nahi.'),
('Pehle many probes, baad mein one probe', 'Screen ne research comparison ke liye multiple methods/settings run kiye. Stage B diagnostic selection per fraction two caps x three repeats = six probe attempts charge karti thi, plus preparation once. Us replay ka median profiling cost 24.62 s (1/8) aur 26.38 s (1/4) tha. One-probe study ne poocha: six ki jagah sirf ek ho toh viable hai? Answer current records mein phir bhi no benefit.'),
('Repeated runs aur real request', 'Experiment repeats variability samajhne ke liye hain. Actual one-probe decision ko same request ke three repeats dekhkar median choose karne ki permission nahi. Each diagnostic decision one observation dekhti hai. Shared sample preparation ko every hypothetical request mein charge kiya; development repeats mein amortize karke artificial savings nahi dikhayi.'),
('Purani 10.96-second baat', 'Chat ka 10.96 s quote is PPT ke 10.37 s metric ke saath automatically equate nahi karna. Is guide ke checked evidence mein slide 9 ka exact reported aggregate 10.37 s hai. 10.96 ka specific run/receipt identify kiye bina usko total profiling time, multiple probes ka time ya actual online latency declare nahi kar rahe.'),
('Kya total cost fully known hai?', 'Metadata/controller wall overhead aur sample preparation ka full CPU/RAM exposure unmeasured hain. Reported resource-time is configured proxy, actual utilization ya currency nahi. Persisting cluster ya reusing samples future comparison ko change karega; baselines ko bhi same reuse benefit dena padega.'), refs=('R4','R7'))

page(10, '143 tests aur 38 tests: kya verify hua?',
('Original-advisor software checkpoint', 'Implementation d6f906a par original Windows .venv, Python 3.14.6: 143 passed, zero failed/errors/skipped, 36.89 s. pip check passed. Full suite mein tiny Dask integration fixtures the. Yeh historical receipt caa8a8a mein published hai, model ki 143 successful research experiments ka count nahi.'),
('Research contract checkpoint', 'One-probe implementation 82d40af ke Windows check mein 38 tests passed, 0.23 s test-suite time. Existing records par eight default decisions, 24 single-observation counterfactual decisions aur 37 termination records ki memory representation check hui. Published evidence reference 7f9c1b0 hai. Koi new Dask workload/pilot execute nahi hua.'),
('Counts ko add karke claim kyun nahi?', '143 aur 38 separate branches/suites/checkpoints ke counts hain. They answer software behavior questions. Inhe 181 independent scientific experiments, 100% advisor accuracy ya all future inputs supported nahi bolte. Test passing requirements ke checked examples par code behavior establish karta hai.'),
('78 hashes kya hain?', 'Original receipt source/evidence files ke fingerprints retain karti hai. Isse tested version trace hota hai. Later report audit mein runtime.py ka explanatory docstring change hua; executable AST unchanged verify hua, but current byte hash differs. Old 143 receipt still original tested checkpoint ka evidence hai; usko silently latest bytes ka test certificate nahi banate.'),
('PPT par bolne ke liye', '"Software verification complete hai. Experiment verification abhi separate next step hai. Small test fixtures aur historical replays fresh 96-cell study nahi hain." Slide par zero fresh cells isi difference ko explicitly show karta hai. Test wall seconds ko benchmark runtime comparisons mein mix nahi karte.'), refs=('M7','M12','R8'))

page(10, 'Prospective validation: next 96 runs ka process',
('Prospective ka meaning', 'Pehle prediction aur selection record karo; phir future execution ka outcome collect karo; finally compare karo. Retrospective replay mein old outcome table reuse hoti hai. Same original four inputs par fresh runs new observations hain, lekin new unseen workload generalization test nahi.'),
('Step 1: checkpoint aur study freeze', 'User evidence review ke baad suitable current software verification receipt chahiye. Current source/receipt fingerprint mismatch ho toh new suffixed verification output lo; old receipt edit mat karo. Dataset hashes, model, configs, deadlines aur pre-run advice freeze karo. This guide sirf workflow samjhati hai; koi prepare/run command execute nahi ki.'),
('Step 2: bounded physical collection', 'Four profiles x eight configs x three repeats = 96 planned attempts. Original Windows host, consistent power/background-load conditions, separate study directory aur append-only journal use honge. Every start/outcome save hoga. Failed, interrupted ya timed-out attempt hide/retry karke result improve nahi karna.'),
('Step 3: independent evaluator', 'Saved predictions versus fresh successful runtimes ka error/upper coverage; actual deadline outcomes; selected config aur fixed baselines ke configured resource-time proxies; all failures/unknowns with denominators. Acceptance out of four profiles aur selected outcomes out of at most twelve runs separately report honge.'),
('Abhi ki status line', '"Windows software verification complete hai; fresh 96-run study planned hai aur execution pending hai." Local status docs mein study prepared/started nahi. No fresh validation results exist in checked output locations. Kisi future run se claim change ho toh actual receipt first update karna, slide expectation ko result mat bana dena.'), refs=('M1','M7','M12'))

page(11, 'Limitations: kaunsa claim defend kar sakte ho?',
('Supported scope', 'Original advisor four fixed synthetic profiles aur eight declared settings par bounded hai. One Windows host par results hain. Unknown size/layout/host par blanket promise nahi. Current original data mein all 96 runs successful hone se failure-probability training ke labels nahi mile; failure_probability null hone ka yahi reason hai.'),
('34.1% figure ka exact meaning', 'Older recommend-model policy ka mean median normalized resource-time proxy 7.524 versus declared reference 11.421 tha. (11.421 - 7.524)/11.421 about 34.1%. Same historical table reused hui; some rows model fitting source thi. Yeh independent fresh savings, electricity reduction ya cloud bill reduction nahi.'),
('Older aur newer objectives', '34.1% old objective ke historical replay se hai. New balanced advise ka J different normalized formula hai. Old savings ko new balanced policy ka achieved gain bolna wrong attribution hoga. Slide "earlier cost comparison" isi distinction ke liye important hai.'),
('Research ne kya achieve kiya?', 'Measured negative finding: quiet samples tested full-pressure cases miss karte hain. Worker evidence ne saved-peak under-observation reveal ki. Continuous signal metadata choices improve nahi kar paya; one probe ka economics unfavorable tha. Yeh useful measurement/decision evidence hai, proven novel universal algorithm nahi.'),
('Ek strong honest conclusion', '"Humne advisor implement kiya aur bounded runtime-prediction result establish kiya. Research mein probe ki information aur cost dono test kiye. Current short-workload use case mein probing justify nahi hui, isliye usko disabled rakha. Fresh prospective validation next hai."'), refs=('M2','M4','M13','R4','R6','R7'))

page(11, 'Aage ka plan: product aur research alag tracks',
('Original advisor track', 'Fresh 96-run validation ko predeclared protocol se execute/evaluate karna. Saved advice ko exact verified input execution se bind karna. Local UI banana jahan recommendation, rejection reason aur measured outcome clearly linked hon. UI banana scientific accuracy improve karna nahi, usability/integration milestone hai.'),
('Broader support track', 'New sizes, partition layouts, seeds aur maybe hardware collect karne se pehle versioned feature/data contract chahiye. Current frozen support gate bypass karke arbitrary workload accept nahi karna. New model/calibration aur untouched workload-group evaluation chahiye. More repeats same few inputs ka scope automatically broaden nahi karte.'),
('Research probe track', 'Specific hypothesis chahiye ki kis meaningful workload par probe metadata se different aur better decision dega. Profiling cost ka budget predeclare karo; strong fixed/metadata/analytical baselines rakho. Longer jobs ya repeated-job reuse possible directions hain, completed results nahi. Untouched seeds useful hain, but already inspected recipes ke new seeds alone broad generalization proof nahi.'),
('Kya automatically start nahi hoga?', 'Old Stage C, disabled 48-attempt one-probe draft, arbitrary training ya main merge current guide ka part nahi. Research gate failed ho toh sirf more rows collect karke contribution claim nahi ban jata. First useful hypothesis aur affordable evaluation design.'),
('Presentation ka closing sentence', '"Next hum fresh execution evidence se original advisor validate karenge. Research side par additional memory signal ko tabhi pursue karenge jab woh metadata se extra benefit de aur measurement ka kharcha recover kar sake." Isse ambition bhi clear hai aur current evidence ki boundary bhi.'), refs=('M1','M7','R7','R9'))

page(12, 'Numbers ka one-page revision map',
('Original advisor', '<b>4:</b> fixed workload profiles. <b>8:</b> candidate configurations. <b>32:</b> family/config groups. <b>96:</b> original physical runs. <b>36/36/24:</b> train/calibration/test rows. <b>12/12/8:</b> corresponding groups. <b>13.84%:</b> held-out LightGBM MdAPE, not training accuracy. <b>23.01%:</b> baseline MdAPE. <b>1.688:</b> upper multiplier. <b>24/24:</b> observed test-row coverage.'),
('Research screen aur Stage A', '<b>768:</b> earlier screen attempts = 192 full + 576 probes. <b>759/1/8:</b> success/timeout/error. <b>48:</b> Stage A full attempts. <b>41/7:</b> successes/errors. <b>17/24:</b> low-cap successes. <b>24/24:</b> high-cap successes. Stage A ke 48 ko disabled future 48-attempt pilot samajhna wrong hai.'),
('Stage B aur memory', '<b>96:</b> Stage B probes, all quiet success. <b>32:</b> instance/cap/fraction comparison groups. <b>8:</b> pressure discrepancies = four low-cap cases x two fractions. <b>144:</b> Stage A+B total jobs. <b>321:</b> retained worker lifetimes. <b>37:</b> lifetimes with termination events. <b>33/37:</b> sampled peak below threshold. <b>36/37:</b> event RSS above sampled peak.'),
('Cost aur tests', '<b>4.79 s:</b> metadata-associated reconstructed request median. <b>10.37 s:</b> always-one-probe reconstructed median. <b>5.47 s:</b> single-probe prep/lifecycle/preflight median. <b>143:</b> main Windows software tests. <b>38:</b> research tests. <b>0:</b> fresh validation cells executed in checked status. <b>96:</b> pending fresh validation attempts.'),
('Revision trick', 'Har number ke saath teen sawaal bolo: kis study ka? kis unit ka? denominator kya? Agar tum yeh teen answer kar paate ho toh most viva confusions solve ho jaate hain. Across studies repeated numbers coincidence ho sakte hain; unhe ek combined accuracy metric mat banao.'), refs=('M2','M3','M7','R1','R3','R4','R6','R7','R8'))

page(12, 'Viva practice: questions aur short Hinglish answers',
('Q1. Humne ML kyun use kiya?', 'Configuration aur workload descriptors se runtime estimate chahiye tha. LightGBM ko tabular regression option ke roop mein use kiya; simple family-median baseline ke against lower held-out error mila. Har alternative se superior prove nahi kiya.'),
('Q2. Probe ko choose kaise kiya?', 'Initial screen ne uniform, memory-scaled uniform aur partition-tail compare kiye. Later Stage B ne memory-scaled uniform at 1/8 aur 1/4 se pressure fidelity check ki. Continuous quarter-sample signal mein wider development separation thi, toh one-probe counterfactual investigate hua. Final admission phir bhi disabled raha because no extra choice benefit and cost.'),
('Q3. Successful sample se full safety kyun nahi?', 'Smaller input, scaled cap aur full join dimension ke memory effects exactly proportional nahi. Tested sample signals quiet the jab full run pressured tha. Humne exact mechanism fully isolate nahi kiya, lekin mismatch directly measured hai.'),
('Q4. 143 tests pass toh experiment pending kyun?', 'Tests software contracts/tiny fixtures verify karte hain. Fresh study actual current timings and selection outcomes collect karegi. Correct code aur beneficial real-world recommendation separate questions hain.'),
('Q5. Model ka training accuracy kitna?', 'Main quoted number held-out MdAPE 13.84% hai. Separate training-accuracy figure is evidence mein report nahi hui. Regression error ko classification accuracy mein convert nahi karte.'),
('Q6. Aapka contribution kya hai?', 'A constrained explainable configuration advisor, controlled local measurements, and a separate investigation showing limits and cost of small-sample memory signals. Universal failure prediction, new best ML method ya cloud-scale validation claim nahi.'), refs=('M3','M4','M7','R1','R4','R7'))

page(12, 'Puri presentation ki connected speaking script',
('Opening: slides 1-3', '"Data job ko resources dene mein trade-off hai: kam resources se slow/failure risk, zyada se configured burden. SAFE-Pipe known workload profiles ke liye deadline-aware setting recommend karta hai. Offline benchmark se model fit hota hai; request par saved model predictions aur checks use hote hain. Research prototype separate hai."'),
('Original result: slides 4-6', '"Humne four frozen profiles par eight settings ko three times run kiya: 96 executions. Same family/config ke repeats split mein saath rakhe. Test MdAPE baseline 23.01% se LightGBM 13.84% tha; upper estimates all 24 held-out rows cover karte the, limited scope ke andar. Balanced score time aur configured resources trade off karta hai; sort example mein 2 GB total option choose hua."'),
('Research: slides 7-8', '"Midterm ke baad humne full-versus-sample behavior study kiya. Stage A mein 48 full attempts mein seven errors low cap par the. Stage B ke 96 smaller probes all quiet the, phir bhi eight comparison groups mein full pressure miss hua. Worker telemetry ne dikhaya ki saved periodic peak termination-time higher RSS ko miss kar sakti hai."'),
('Decision: slides 9-10', '"Continuous probe ratios useful separation dikhate the, but stronger metadata same choices de rahi thi. One-probe replay ne median constructed time 4.79 se 10.37 seconds badhaya. Isliye automatic probing disabled hai. Original and research code ke software checks passed hain; fresh prospective experiments abhi pending hain."'),
('Close: slide 11', '"Current result one host aur fixed workloads tak bounded hai. Old 34.1% resource proxy difference historical replay hai. Next step fresh predictions-first validation, exact-input execution binding aur UI hai. Probe research ko tab continue karenge jab extra information aur total-cost benefit ka specific reason ho."'),
('Practice ka tareeka', 'Pehle script apne words mein bolo, phir notes band karke ek simple example do. Formula ratne se pehle explain karo ki each quantity kis cheez ko represent karti hai. Agar exact mechanism nahi measured, "we have not isolated that yet" bolna correct scientific answer hai.'), refs=('M1','M3','M4','R3','R4','R6','R7'))
